<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2606.14047v1/img/latency_throughput_comparison.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/199;" width="476" height="199" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>
Speed performance comparison showing:
(a) <span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Per-token latency</span> demonstrating KGERMAR’s consistent processing time (0.43-0.91ms) versus baselines’ scaling;
(b) <span id="A1.F5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Throughput</span> highlighting KGERMAR’s stable token generation (1.1-2.3K tokens/sec) despite higher absolute latency.
Error bars represent standard deviation across 5 runs.
</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Implementation Notes</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{consolidate}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>consolidate</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{consolidate}()</annotation></semantics></math> function merges entities using:</p>
<table id="A1.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{Merge}(e_{i},e_{j})\iff" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Merge</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇔</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{Merge}(e_{i},e_{j})\iff</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{sim}_{string}(e_{i},e_{j})&gt;\theta_{str}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>sim</mtext><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{sim}_{string}(e_{i},e_{j})&gt;\theta_{str}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lor\;\text{sim}_{embed}(e_{i},e_{j})&gt;\theta_{ctx}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∨</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>sim</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lor\;\text{sim}_{embed}(e_{i},e_{j})&gt;\theta_{ctx}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sim}_{string}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>sim</mtext><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sim}_{string}</annotation></semantics></math> uses fuzzy string matching (Levenshtein distance), <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sim}_{embed}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext>sim</mtext><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sim}_{embed}</annotation></semantics></math> computes cosine similarity between entity embeddings from the base language model, and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{str}=0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{str}=0.85</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{ctx}=0.90" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.90</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{ctx}=0.90</annotation></semantics></math> are thresholds determined through validation.
The <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}()" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}()</annotation></semantics></math> function computes token-level distance as <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Dist}(e_{h},e_{t})=\min(|s_{h}-s_{t}|,|s_{h}-t_{t}|,|t_{h}-s_{t}|,|t_{h}-t_{t}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Dist</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Dist}(e_{h},e_{t})=\min(|s_{h}-s_{t}|,|s_{h}-t_{t}|,|t_{h}-s_{t}|,|t_{h}-t_{t}|)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{h},t_{h})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{h},t_{h})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{t},t_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{t},t_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> are entity positions. The frequency score <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(FS)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(FS)</annotation></semantics></math> balances confidence with occurrence patterns:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{FS}(h,r,t)=\text{count}(h,r,t)/\max_{(h^{\prime},r^{\prime},t^{\prime})}\text{count}(h^{\prime},r^{\prime},t^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>FS</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>count</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mtext>count</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>h</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{FS}(h,r,t)=\text{count}(h,r,t)/\max_{(h^{\prime},r^{\prime},t^{\prime})}\text{count}(h^{\prime},r^{\prime},t^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Latency and Throughput Analysis</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate the speed characteristics of KGERMAR against ERMAR and MemLong across context lengths from 1K to 32K tokens on the PG-19 dataset (NVIDIA L40S GPU). Table <a href="#A2.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Appendix B Latency and Throughput Analysis ‣ Knowledge Graph Enhanced Memory-Augmented Retrieval for Long Context Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ A.2 Multi-Modal Retrieval ‣ Appendix A Algorithmic Details ‣ Knowledge Graph Enhanced Memory-Augmented Retrieval for Long Context Modeling" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> reveal the fundamental tradeoffs between our memory-optimized architecture and conventional approaches.</p>
</div>
